 added it to link and if i were  learning  and i'm going to show you because i got  some software called loom which enables  me to show you what i'm doing on my  computer so i went through a  demonstration of using this gisho kanji  and then when i looked at my video i  realized that the loom doesn't capture a  pop-up  so therefore i will show you  some of the other things i do on our  website or that i would do if i were  learning japanese but i can't show you  the pop-up so i'll simply explain that  the dicho kanji pop-up comes up  uh since most words in japanese and  chinese are actually combinations of  kanji  so for example uh totsuzen suddenly  is totsu and zen totsuzen  and so jishukanji goes through each one  of these characters provides a lot of  information about the character  uh you know they sort of call it the  japanese style pronunciation the chinese  origin pronunciation  uh how important the character this is  difficulty level it shows you the stroke  order and it does it for each one of  these so that  if you are using link which i recommend  obviously that's what i like to use and  you come across characters every time  you come across it you can look it up in  this  dictionary and you can once again be  reminded of the range of meanings and  how it's used and its importance in  stroke and so on and if you keep on  doing that eventually they are going to  stick  uh you should also read about you know  some of the components of characters you  know the the the  water symbol the metal one or gold and  all these different things that reappear  as components of the characters and you  can go and find a book on that and you  should acquaint yourself  with these things even though initially  it's going to be  not so meaningful until you've been  exposed to a lot of characters it's like  grammar you  have to combine the exposure with some  degree of  explanation but put more emphasis on the  exposure rather than on the explanation  now the other thing that i would do  other than a lot of reading and frequent  lookups in this gisha kanji  is that i would avail myself of the  dictation function that we have at link  and i'll make a brief demonstration of  that with my screenshot  screencast here but that simply means  that you would set  your uh activities  to those are the review activities and  link you would set them to dictation and  not do the closed test or not do the  flash card just do the dictation  and if you are on a computer you have to  set your keyboard  to japanese if you are on an ipad or an  iphone  then within the link system it'll  automatically  go to a japanese keyboard if you have  that keyboard set up on your ipad or  portable device android whatever it  might be  uh and then you will hear the  text-to-speech pronunciation of a word  tortuzen and you will then be required  to type it  and then you will see the character pop  up  uh  and all of this is going to help you and  i should add that just the mere fact  that we have um  uh you know um  word processing softwares on our  computers whereby we type in a romanized  form of japanese and a number of  characters are suggested for us it's  another way of reviewing the characters  so technology makes it much easier  to learn  characters today you should still  get a book  which explains some of the components i  mean it's a matter of where your  interests lie  but make it a major project to learn the  characters  learn them as a part of your input  reading activities  and uh and  you know  bit by bit you know it seems like an  enormous tax task two thousand  characters but if you slice it off  salami style  going at it gradually gradually building  up forgetting relearning forgetting  relearning  you will eventually  become familiar  familiar enough with the characters  to read in my opinion and i think it's  something well worth doing and uh i will  show you briefly because i'm keen on  using this new software that i've got  how i would do that 